			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement Tauri command stubs for TreeView lifecycle\n\nIntroduce a complete set of Tauri IPC commands for the TreeView subsystem within the Mountain backend, fulfilling the `Common` library contract for tree-based UI interactions. This addition bridges the Sky frontend with the native environment to support hierarchical data rendering and navigation.\n\nImplemented commands include:\n- **Data Retrieval:** `GetTreeViewChildren` and `GetTreeViewItem` to fetch tree structure and metadata via `CommonTreeViewProvider`.\n- **Navigation & Refresh:** `RevealTreeViewItem` (scroll/focus) and `RefreshTreeView` (partial or full tree updates).\n- **State Management (Stubs):** `PersistTreeView` and `RestoreTreeView` for session restoration, and `OnTreeViewExpansionChanged`/`OnTreeViewSelectionChanged` for event-driven logic. These are currently implemented as no-ops returning explicit error messages, with TODOs to wire them into the provider trait for future implementation.\n\nThe implementation follows the project's effect-based architecture, retrieving the `MountainEnvironment` via the `ApplicationRunTime` and dispatching calls to the required `CommonTreeViewProvider` instance. This lays the groundwork for feature parity with VS Code's tree view capabilities in the native substrate.",
			"SHA": "99d6d9fc94fbbf93aa11061c85f15b834fcb0e6e"
		}
